<box type="9">
  Yoh finds herself sitting alone in the cafeteria, searching for a familiar face as her lunch cools on the table in front of her.<K>
  She was hoping to see Koji today, but he must have had other plans. That wouldn't be at all unusual. Normally, Omi and Fuminori would pick up the slack.<K>
  But Omi and Fuminori aren't here anymore.

  Yoh puts down her chopsticks, her appetite ruined by the lack of company―and by the anxiety eating at her.<K> Omi is missing, Fuminori has turned on her, and she has no idea why.<K>
  If Koji were here, she could count on him to distract her with some idle conversation.

  Now that she is all by herself, Yoh becomes keenly aware of how little tolerance she has for loneliness.<K>
  She begins to feel paranoid, like the whole world is plotting to take from her everything that she cherishes.<K>
  What is going on here?<K> Where has Omi gone?<K> Is Fuminori really unrelated to her disappearance?<K>
  Or is he the key to this mystery, as Koji and Dr. Tanbo suspect?


